       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than twice the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day. Each 3,000 mg dose is also three times the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. At that level there is a serious risk of hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1000 mg by mouth three times daily**, which is 3,000 mg/day.\n- **1000 mg by mouth four times daily**, which is 4,000 mg/day. This is the standard maximum, and many clinicians use a lower ceiling of 3,000 mg/day.\n- **650 mg by mouth every 6 hours**, which is 2,600 mg/day.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want the original order, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
