       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. A 9,000 mg/day dose of acetaminophen risks severe liver injury or death. You haven't given a clinical rationale that would justify it, and I don't know of one. Normal liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't make it safe.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day)\n- Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily (4,000 mg/day, the maximum)\n- Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours (2,600 mg/day)\n\nIf the aim is stronger pain control, I can enter a multimodal regimen instead. Your pharmacist can help you build one. If you think a higher dose is truly warranted, please review it with pharmacy or toxicology first, and enter it through a pathway that has a second clinical check.\n\nWhich of these would you like me to enter?"
      }
